# Benchmark Pulse configuration.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" in the same folder and fill in ONE provider key.
# The app detects which one is present and uses it; no other change is needed.
#
# Treat .env as a secret. Do not share it or paste it into chat or a deck.

# --- Option 1: Google Gemini (recommended: free tier, no credit card) --------
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Leave blank for the sensible default.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest

# --- Option 2: Groq (also free, fastest responses) --------------------------
# Get a key at https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- Option 3: Anthropic ----------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Option 4: Azure OpenAI (the production path for Preferred Square) ------
# Client data stays inside the firm's own Azure tenant. Swapping to this is the
# only change required to move from pilot to firmwide deployment.
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4o-mini

# --- Force a specific provider ---------------------------------------------
# Set to: gemini | groq | anthropic | azure_openai | stub
# "stub" runs the whole pipeline with no model at all, using templates.
# BENCHMARK_PULSE_LLM=

# --- SEC EDGAR (US IPO filings) --------------------------------------------
# The SEC requires a real contact address in the User-Agent header and returns
# 403 without one. Use a firm address, not a personal mailbox.
# SEC_CONTACT_EMAIL=
